extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 75-76 (cache p075-p076, page_offset 0). The abilities, attribute requirement and first skills are printed 75; the rest of the O.C.C. Skills, the related list, secondary skills, equipment and money run onto printed 76. Printed 75 checked against a 200 dpi render; OCR and render agree. || RACE: the Arkhon R.C.C. (printed 72) says the tiny percentage of master psionics become Arkhon ESP Specialists, and this class opens with Language and Literacy: Arkhon at 98%; stored as race_restrictions only arkhon. Written as an ADDITION to the Arkhon R.C.C. (the Pucara Mind Mage convention): named skills restated, held once. The printed Language: One of choice (+15%) is NOT restated, because the race already grants a two-language +15% group and choice groups from both halves stay separate; an ESP Specialist therefore ends up with the race''s two languages rather than the printed one - recorded, not fixed. The race''s Running, Pilot of choice (+10%) and W.P. Sword-or-Knife pick also carry into the pairing although the O.C.C. list does not print them; composition cannot drop a race''s skills without supersedes_race, and the book does not say the character stops being an Arkhon. || MASTER PSIONIC REQUIREMENT: printed as Attribute Requirements: M.E. 14 or higher; master psionic. The M.E. 14 is enforced; the master-psionic condition is a restriction line - the app cannot gate an occupation on a psionics roll, and the class states its own master block, so a character taking it does not roll. || XP: the ESP Specialist ladder on printed 192, as briefed. || GROUP: psychic - a master psionic trained by its family, the group every mind-mage-shaped O.C.C. carries. No sdc_base or mdc_base; men_of_arms: false (a psychic, not a men-of-arms heading - the book files no O.C.C. under a group heading); the race''s 2D6x10 S.D.C. bonus always applies because the class cannot be taken without it. || PSIONICS: master; I.S.P. 2D6x10 + M.E., +10 per additional level. The seven printed Sensitive powers granted by name: Empathy, Mind Block, Presence Sense, See Aura, See the Invisible (catalog See The Invisible), Sense Magic, Telepathy. The book calls all seven sensitive; the catalog files Mind Block under Physical, which does not matter for a named grant. Other Powers is an EITHER/OR - two Physical or Healing powers, OR one Super power - so it is a special_abilities choice whose two options each carry a psionics block with its own powers_starting and starting group; an ability''s psionics merge over the class''s (ladder keys from the ability, counts the higher), and neither option states powers_schedule, so the class''s schedule survives. Per level from 2: one Sensitive power plus one power of any category, as two schedule entries per level (2-15). categories_allowed Sensitive, Physical, Healing, Super (any category). The race states no psionics block, so nothing else merges. || BONUSES: printed +1 initiative, +1 roll with impact, +3 pull punch, +5 save vs Horror Factor, ''considered a master psionic''. Judgement, the same as the Spectral Hunter: the O.C.C. block restates the race''s line with new figures (the race gives +1 initiative, +2 roll, +2 pull punch, +3 vs Horror Factor), and bonuses sum across a pairing, so only the difference to the printed figures is stored: roll -1 (2 - 1 = the printed 1), pull_punch +1 (2 + 1 = 3), horror_factor +2 (3 + 2 = 5); initiative adds nothing. The race''s +2 save vs magic carries through. The master-psionic save target follows the psionics tier. || SKILLS: Arkhon 98 and literacy 98 restated; Computer Operation 40+15 = 55; Radio: Basic 45+15 = 60; Intelligence 32+10 = 42 (per level 4, the catalog''s); Interrogation (Espionage row) 30+10 = 40 - the Military Interrogation Techniques row is a different skill; W.P. Energy Rifle, W.P. Energy Pistol, W.P. Knife; Hand to Hand: Basic, which replaces the race''s Expert because a later grant wins; hand_to_hand costs expert 1, martial_arts 2, assassin 2 as printed (no alignment condition printed). || RELATED: printed as R.C.C. Related Skills (a slip: the class is an O.C.C.); 6, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9, 11 and 13. All Any: Communications +10, Electrical +5, Espionage +10, Mechanical +5, Medical +10 (''often selected for methods of torture'', a note), Military +5, Pilot Related +5, Rogue +5, Science +5, Technical +10; Domestic, Physical, Pilot, W.P. and Wilderness none. Secondary: 5. These replace the race''s lists in a pairing. || EQUIPMENT: printed as the race''s list plus a hand computer and recorder, torture tools (knives, scalpels, a laser scalpel, picks, needles, clamps, and a medical kit if a doctor) and 1D4 pairs of handcuffs. Equipment sums across a pairing, so only the additions are stored: hand-held-computer, pocket-digital-disc-recorder (judgement: ''recorder'' unqualified), scalpel and laser-scalpel for the torture kit, handcuffs-regular x1D4. The medical kit ''if a doctor'' is conditional and not stored. The rifle, pistol, armor, communicator, survival kit, survival knife and archaic-or-modern weapon come from the race. || MONEY: 2D6x1000 Arkhon credits stored as printed; in a pairing the race''s 1D6x1000 wins by the composition rule, so this figure shows on the class detail only. || Alignment (45% miscreant, 25% aberrant, 10% diabolic, 15% anarchist, 5% other) and allies are GM notes and lore."
---

## Lore

Many Arkhons have some psychic talent, but only a handful are true master
psionics, and the great families groom these few carefully as elite scouts,
spies and warriors. They serve in small fireteams attached to larger units,
where their job is counter-intelligence and protection against magic: Arkhon
armies face sorcerous nations and supernatural beings, and the specialists are
trained to sense such powers before an assassin or spy can strike.

Ordinary humans fare no better under their empathy and telepathy, which dig
out the truth with ease, and each specialist also has a few stronger powers
for dealing with enemies directly. Some are posted to the Interrogation
Squads, the army''s dreaded questioners, where the mind succeeds where torture
fails.

## GM Notes

Alignment: 45% miscreant, 25% aberrant, 10% diabolic, 15% anarchist, 5% other.
